# OpenAI Ads Pixel — GTM Tag Template
Version: 1.2.0
Author: Custom Template
Last Updated: 2026-05-07

## Overview
This template loads the OpenAI Ads Measurement Pixel SDK and fires conversion
events from Google Tag Manager. It supports four event modes:

1. **Standard Events** — Map directly to OpenAI's supported event taxonomy
   (order_created, checkout_started, etc.) with manual parameter entry.

2. **Custom Events** — Fire `oaiq("measure", "custom", ...)` with your own
   `custom_event_name`. Must be lowercase, 1–64 chars, no built-in name conflicts.

3. **GA4 / Enhanced Ecommerce (Auto-map)** — No configuration needed. The tag
   reads the `event` key from the dataLayer to determine which GA4 event fired,
   maps it to the corresponding OpenAI event name, and reads ecommerce.value,
   ecommerce.currency, ecommerce.items[], and ecommerce.transaction_id
   automatically.

4. **GTM Variable** — Drive the event name from any GTM variable (e.g. {{Event}}).
   The resolved value must match an OpenAI standard event name or 'custom'.

## GA4 Ecommerce Mapping (auto, no dropdown needed)
| GA4 event         | OpenAI event           | Data shape       |
|-------------------|------------------------|------------------|
| page_view         | page_viewed            | contents         |
| view_item         | contents_viewed        | contents         |
| view_item_list    | contents_viewed        | contents         |
| add_to_cart       | items_added            | contents         |
| begin_checkout    | checkout_started       | contents         |
| purchase          | order_created          | contents         |
| generate_lead     | lead_created           | customer_action  |
| sign_up           | registration_completed | customer_action  |

GA4 dataLayer field mappings:
  dataLayer event key          → GA4_EVENT_MAP lookup → OpenAI event name
  ecommerce.value × 100        → eventProps.amount (integer cents)
  ecommerce.currency           → eventProps.currency
  ecommerce.items[]            → eventProps.contents[]
    item_id / id               →   contents[].id
    item_name / name           →   contents[].name
    item_category              →   contents[].content_type
    quantity                   →   contents[].quantity
    price × 100                →   contents[].amount
  ecommerce.transaction_id     → eventOptions.event_id

## Contents Items (MAP type — inline rows, no pop-up)
Each row is a parameter → value pair rendered inline. Select the parameter
from the left dropdown and type the value (or a GTM variable) in the right
text field. For multiple products, repeat the full set of fields starting with
a new `id` row — the JS groups items by detecting when the `id` key repeats.

Example for two products:
  id           | sku_1
  name         | Widget A
  quantity     | 1
  amount       | 2599
  id           | sku_2          ← second id starts a new item
  name         | Widget B
  quantity     | 2

## Amount Handling
OpenAI requires amounts as integers in the currency's lowest denomination
(e.g., cents for USD). GA4 mode multiplies ecommerce.value and item.price × 100
automatically. In Standard/Custom/Variable mode, enter amounts already as
integers (e.g. enter 2599 for $25.99).

## Deduplication (Event ID section)
Supply the same event_id on both the pixel and your server-side Conversions API
call to prevent double-counting. GA4 mode uses ecommerce.transaction_id
automatically. The pixel SDK auto-generates an ID if none is provided.

## Debug Mode
Enable during testing to see pixel activity in the browser console.
Disable before going live.

## Required Permissions
- inject_script: loads https://bzrcdn.openai.com/sdk/oaiq.min.js
- read_data_layer: reads event name and ecommerce object (GA4 mode)
- access_globals: reads/writes window.oaiq and window.oaiq.q
- logging: console output in debug mode only


